  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Morning Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    02 August 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good morning Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,217.50/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,216.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>EMADEB</td>\n                <td>₦1,217.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,216.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SIGMUND</td>\n                <td>₦1,222.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SHEMA</td>\n                <td>₦1,216.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,216.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ARDOVA</td>\n                <td>₦1,217.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SOROMAN</td>\n                <td>₦1,220.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,640.12/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,651.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>TMDK</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>WOSBAB</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>EMADEB</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>T.TIME</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AITEO</td>\n                <td>₦1,640.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>GULF TREASURE</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Nigeria's Domestic Gas Supply Misses Target by 35% Despite 2.05bcf Daily Deliveries\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria delivered an average of 2.05 billion standard cubic feet (Bscf) of gas per day to the domestic market during the first half of 2026. The volume still fell 35 per cent short of the country's Domestic Gas Delivery Obligation. The shortfall of about 1.11 Bscf daily continues to limit gas availability for electricity generation, industrial manufacturing and other strategic sectors of the economy.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nigerias-domestic-gas-supply-misses-target-by-35-despite-205bcf-daily-deliveries\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Depot Prices Weekly Review: 27th – 31st July 2026\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria's downstream petroleum market extended its bearish momentum during the final trading week of July. Depot prices for Premium Motor Spirit (PMS) and Automotive Gas Oil (AGO) declined across most major supply hubs. The broad-based price moderation reflected improved product availability and increased competition among private depot owners.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/depot-prices-weekly-review-27th-31st-july-2026\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Vessel Arrivals: Matrix, Ardova, Stockgap, Others Receive Fresh PMS, AGO, LPG Cargoes\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Fresh petroleum cargoes continue to arrive at Nigeria's major coastal depots as downstream operators intensify stock replenishment efforts. The latest tanker position report monitored by Petroleumprice.ng shows a steady flow of Premium Motor Spirit (PMS), Automotive Gas Oil (AGO) and Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) into Lagos, Warri, Port Harcourt and Calabar between July 26 and July 31.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/vessel-arrivals-matrix-ardova-stockgap-others-receive-fresh-pms-ago-lpg-cargoes\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NNPCL Posts ₦535bn June Profit, Remits ₦6.3tn to Federation Accounts\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Nigerian National Petroleum Company Limited (NNPC Ltd.) posted a profit after tax of ₦535 billion in June 2026. This was despite a marginal decline in crude oil and condensate production during the period. The company attributed the marginal production decline to operational disruptions and facility integrity challenges.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nnpcl-posts-535bn-june-profit-remits-63tn-to-federation-accounts\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Brent Crude Returns to $90 as Fresh Iran Strikes Renew Supply Fears\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude traded at $90.02 per barrel on Friday, up 1.11 percent. West Texas Intermediate (WTI) rose 1.64 percent to $84.96 per barrel. Despite Friday's gains, both Brent and WTI remain below the peaks recorded earlier this year.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/brent-crude-returns-to-90-as-fresh-iran-strikes-renew-supply-fears\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
